  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "If the vertex of the conic $y^{2}-4 y=4 x-4 a$ always lies between the straight lines ${x}+y=3$ and $2 x+2 y-1=0,$ then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "LGL74",
      "text": "$2    < a < 4$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ukkIz",
      "text": "$-\\frac{1}{2}    < a < 2$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cDVtu",
      "text": "$0    < a < 2$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lJGfY",
      "text": "$-\\frac{1}{2}    < a < \\frac{3}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Equation of the vertex of conic\r\n$$\r\ny^{2}-4 y=4 x-4 a\r\n$$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad y^{2}-4 y+4=4 x-4 a+4$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad(y-2)^{2}=4[x-(a-1)]$\r\n$\\therefore$\r\nVertex $=(a-12)$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2016_mat_a40.png\">\r\n\r\nFrom figure,\r\nclearly. $-\\frac{3}{2} < a-1 < 1$\r\n$\\therefore$\r\n$-\\frac{1}{2} < a < 2$",
    "image": null
  },
